<title>JAPAN: Japan August copper imports off 9.3 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan August copper imports off 9.3 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in August totalled 21,211 tonnes, off 9.3 percent from 23,384 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Monday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		  August 96	 July 96	August 95</p>
<p> Total	   21,211	   28,075	  23,384</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	    8,242	   10,493	   8,702</p>
<p> U.S.	     3,008	    4,076	   2,645</p>
<p> Zambia	   4,329	    4,459	   4,234</p>
<p>Imports in the first eight months of 1996 were 241,657 tonnes, against 289,607 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3 3432 6179)</p>
</text>
